 ## Desktop formal audio foundation
 
 - `DesktopVoiceAudioStore` persists immutable MP3 artifacts under the selected root `audio/generated`, with independent ownership/hash receipts, bounded streams and atomic publication. It has no startup orphan sweep; corrupt indexes, missing receipts and unknown files remain preserved. Formal clips use a separate 16 MiB / 30-minute structural/native profile; picker preview stays at its accepted 16 MiB / 120 seconds. Both profiles use the same Windows backend with explicit per-port duration admission.
-- `DesktopVoicePlayback` provides key-independent ordered playback, real MCI pause/position/resume and stop/join. A paused native alias retains the queue and data-operation lease until resume/stop; first UI Stop pauses, second closes. `DesktopChatVoiceRuntime.play` uses current-version placements across later assistant replies in the same session, skipping User turns without TTS (Desktop enhancement). `DesktopAudioFocus` provides separate formal/preview ports over one MCI output; a superseded port cannot stop the current owner. AppContainer owns formal voice drain before preview/native output and root release. Queue admission checks the originating UI foreground token inside the playback mutex; leaving and returning cannot revive a delayed click. Replacement releases a queued/active old voice through native stop before deleting its artifact.
